  "id": "U40",
  "title": "LG Electronics to Build Nvidia AI Server Racks",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-12",
  "article_opening": "By Lee Seok-jin\nLG Electronics (066570.KS) is developing an AI chip-based server rack targeting Nvidia and plans to begin mass production next year. The move expands the recent AI infrastructure alliance between LG and Nvidia into server rack manufacturing.\nAccording to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \"Vera Rubin\" in the first half ",
  "passage": "By Lee Seok-jin\nLG Electronics (066570.KS) is developing an AI chip-based server rack targeting Nvidia and plans to begin mass production next year. The move expands the recent AI infrastructure alliance between LG and Nvidia into server rack manufacturing.\nAccording to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \"Vera Rubin\" in the first half of the year. LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year. The research and development was conducted at a 1.8-megawatt data center cluster established at LG PRI's Pyeongtaek site.\nA compute tray is a module that integrates computing units such as graphics processing units (GPUs) into a single board, with dozens of trays stacked vertically to form a single rack. In the Vera Rubin rack, a total of 108 AI chips operate simultaneously, generating enormous heat, so how quickly and stably the heat is cooled determines the performance of the AI server rack.\nLG Electronics has transferred the cooling technology accumulated over 58 years, since it launched Korea's first home air conditioner in 1968, to its AI racks. Already holding air-cooling and water-co",
  "statement": "LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year."
 },
 {
  "id": "U41",
  "title": "NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-01",
  "article_opening": "It has been reported that, in an effort to break the monopoly of tech giants, NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees for emerging cloud providers by offering GPU computing capacity lease-back arrangements to address their financing challenges. In exchange, NVIDIA will take a revenue share from these cloud providers, directly participating in profit distribution in the downstream computing market and extending its control further down the industrial chain.\nNVIDIA is leveraging its strong balanc",
  "passage": "ion in the downstream computing market and extending its control further down the industrial chain.\nNVIDIA is leveraging its strong balance sheet to gain market leverage, quietly evolving from a chip vendor into the 'central bank' of the AI computing ecosystem by offering financial backing to emerging cloud service providers in exchange for a share of their revenue.\nOn July 1, according to the technology news outlet The Information, NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees to young cloud service providers that lease or rent its GPUs—if these companies fail to secure enough AI developers to rent their computing capacity, NVIDIA will repurchase their unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price.\nIn return, NVIDIA will receive a percentage of these cloud providers’ revenue, with the revenue-sharing rate gradually declining over the term of the contract. GPU cloud providers Firmus and Sharon AI have already joined the program, and three executives with existing business ties to NVIDIA confirmed the arrangement.\nOn July 1, NVIDIA published a statement on its official website announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure, and allowing them to offer computing services to downstream AI-native enterprises, model developers, and corporate clients.\nAccording to the report, the initiative is internally referred to by some NVIDIA personnel as the 'AI Compute Partnership.' A NVIDIA spokesperson also co",
  "statement": "In return, NVIDIA will receive a percentage of these cloud providers’ revenue, with the revenue-sharing rate gradually declining over the term of the contract."
 },
 {
  "id": "U42",
  "title": "DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations GeForce Game Ready Driver Released",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-07",
  "article_opening": "By Andrew Burnes\nOur new GeForce Game Ready Driver optimizes your system for Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced and DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations , launching this week with DLSS.\nHell freezes over in id Software and Bethesda Softworks’ DOOM: The Dark Ages | Revelations , an all-new campaign expansion that unleashes a brutal new chapter of the Slayer’s saga.\nWounded and betrayed, the Slayer is thrust into a merciless purgatory only escapable by confronting haunting truths and forging new st",
  "passage": "rs to sail the Caribbean as Edward Kenway, a rebellious pirate captain drawn into the centuries-old conflict between Assassins and Templars. As Edward pursues glory and fortune, he crosses paths with legendary figures such as Blackbeard, Anne Bonny, and Calico Jack, while the fate of everything the pirates have built hangs in the balance.\nAssassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced is a faithful remake of Assassin’s Creed IV Black Flag , originally released in 2013. Rebuilt from the ground up and powered by the latest Anvil engine, the game features updated visuals and enriched gameplay, including parry‑driven combat, improved stealth and parkour, deeper naval mechanics, and new narrative content.\nLaunching July 9th, the PC release of Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced includes support for ray-traced reflections and ray-traced lighting for realistic reflections, shadows, and water/lighting interactions across the Caribbean, which can be accelerated by DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Frame Generation and Super Resolution on GeForce RTX GPUs.\nAnd via the NVIDIA app, players can upgrade to DLSS 4.5 with the latest DLSS Dynamic Multi Frame Generation and Super Resolution models, for an even faster and more detailed high seas experience.\nLearn more about GeForce Game Ready Drivers here , and download the new GeForce Game Ready 610.74 WHQL driver through the NVIDIA app , or from GeForce.com .",
  "statement": "Launching July 9th, the PC release of Assassin’s Creed Black Flag Resynced includes support for ray-traced reflections and ray-traced lighting for realistic reflections, shadows, and water/lighting interactions across the Caribbean, which can be accelerated by DLSS Multi Frame Generation, Frame Generation and Super Resolution on GeForce RTX GPUs."
 },
