Nvidia has been one of the market's standout long-term performers, evolving from a gaming GPU manufacturer into the world's leading provider of AI infrastructure. Surging demand for AI accelerators and data center chips has fueled a remarkable 984.4% gain in the stock over the past five years, far outpacing the broader market and helping Nvidia become one of the world's most valuable companies. Its dominant position in AI chips and deep partnerships with hyperscale cloud providers have reinforced investor confidence in its long-term growth prospects.
